From: Eloi Rotava <eloi@rotava.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: meson-mx-sdio: register every slot, share the controller

The controller has up to three ports (A, B, C) but the driver only
registered the first "mmc-slot" child.  On the MXQ S805 boxes the Wi-Fi
(SSV6051) is on port A and the SD card slot on port B, so one of them was
always left out.

Every slot now gets its own mmc_host.  The slots take turns on the
controller, one request at a time, from a small queue under the
controller lock; switching ports resets the controller (as the vendor
driver does before every command) and loads the slot's own clock divider
and bus width.  The divider is computed here instead of going through
clk_set_rate(), which sleeps and would touch the hardware while the
other slot is running.

Also:
- MULT and IRQS are written with regmap_write_bits(): both writes have
  side effects (response read-out restart, write-1-to-clear) and must
  not be skipped when the value is unchanged.
- max_blk_count is 256: the hardware field holds "blocks - 1".
- the threaded IRQ only completes the command the hard IRQ saw done,
  so a timeout racing with it cannot complete the next command.

Signed-off-by: Eloi Rotava <eloi@rotava.com>
---
